# EigenScript gap (EigenLua#28): a failed file open gives no reason. Lua's
# luaL_fileresult / errfile append strerror(errno): dofile, loadfile and
# io.open say "cannot open /nonexistent: No such file or directory" (ENOENT)
# or "...: Permission denied" (EACCES). read_text returns "" for a missing
# file, an unreadable one and an empty one alike, and file_exists cannot
# tell ENOENT from EACCES, so the reason cannot be translated; inventing it
# from file_exists would be a substitute (owner decision 1).
# Run as root the unreadable case is readable; run as a user:
#   touch /tmp/f && chmod 000 /tmp/f && eigenscript gaps/no-errno.eigs
# Expected: three different reasons (missing, unreadable, empty).
# Actual v0.45.0 after the touch/chmod setup above, when run as a user:
# ["", false] / ["", true] / ["", true]
write_text of ["/tmp/eigenlua-empty", ""]
for p in ["/nonexistent", "/tmp/f", "/tmp/eigenlua-empty"]:
    print of [read_text of p, file_exists of p]
